    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n25099" root="صهو and صهى" body-key="S">
    
      1 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">صَهَا</span></b>  [or <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">صَهَى</span>], aor. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">يَصْهَىِ</span>, inf. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">صَهْىٌ</span>,
accord. to A'Obeyd; or <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">صَهِىَ</span> accord. to Kh; <i>It</i>
(a wound) <i>was,</i> or <i>became, moist:</i> (S:) or <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">صَهَا</span> or
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">صَهَى</span> [as written in different copies of the K],
aor. 
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">1َ2َ3َ</span></b> ; and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">صَهِىَ</span>; <i>he had a wound and it became
moist.</i> (K.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  And the former, <i>He had much
property.</i> (Az, K.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  And <i>i. q.</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَسَنَّ</span> [<i>He became
advanced in age,</i> or <i>full-grown;</i> &amp;c.]. (TA.)

